xt":"Withdrawn from committee.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-other","code":null,"date":"2025-09-10","eventType":"legislative_action","historyId":"118215923","location":"Assembly","sequence":10,"significance":"routine","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Ordered to third reading.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-passed","code":null,"date":"2025-09-11","eventType":"passed_house","historyId":"118215924","location":"Assembly","sequence":11,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Read third time. Passed. (Ayes 59. Noes 19. Page 3338.) Ordered to the Senate.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-other","code":null,"date":"2025-09-12","eventType":"legislative_action","historyId":"118215925","location":"Senate","sequence":12,"significance":"routine","source":null,"status":null,"text":"In Senate. Concurrence in Assembly amendments pending.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-concurred","code":null,"date":"2025-09-12","eventType":"concurred","historyId":"118215926","location":"Senate","sequence":12,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Assembly amendments concurred in. (Ayes 29. Noes 0. Page 2957.) Ordered to engrossing and enrolling.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-enrolled","code":null,"date":"2025-09-15","eventType":"enrolled","historyId":"118215927","location":"Governor","sequence":13,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Enrolled and presented to the Governor at 2 p.m.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-approved","code":null,"date":"2025-09-17","eventType":"approved_by_governor","historyId":"118215928","location":"Governor","sequence":14,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Approved by the Governor.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-chaptered","code":null,"date":"2025-09-17","eventType":"chaptered","historyId":"118215929","location":"Secretary of State","sequence":15,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Chaptered by Secretary of State. Chapter 115, Statutes of 2025.","time":null,"votes":[]}],"affectedStatutes":[{"action":"IS_AMENDED","code":null,"text":"Section 4 of Chapter 97 of the Statutes of 2025 is amended to read:"}],"approvedDate":"2025-09-17","chapter":{"citation":"Chapter 115, Statutes of 2025","number":"115","type":"CHP","year":"2025"},"chapteredDate":"2025-09-17","committees":[],"conditions":[],"contentHash":"ca3fd456b9ded2549a8ab0bab3667724e634852976205d1ae70dac03994963ea","cosponsorCount":null,"digest":"A special election will be held throughout the state on November 4, 2025. Existing law authorizes consolidation of a local election for the submission of any question, proposition, or office to be filled, which was called by a district, city, or other political subdivision on or before August 8, 2025, and scheduled to be held on November 4, 2025, with the statewide special election. Existing law prohibits a county elections official from certifying the results of the statewide special election before the 28th calendar day following the election.\n\nThis bill would also prohibit a county elections official from certifying the results of a local election called by a district, city, or other political subdivision on or before August 8, 2025, and scheduled to be held on November 4, 2025, before the 28th calendar day following the election.\n\nExisting law requires the Secretary of State to report on the final costs of the statewide special election to the Director of Finance and the Joint Legislative Budget Committee no later than April 1, 2026.\n\nThis bill would appropriate $100,000 from the General Fund to the Secretary of State for purposes of that report.\n\nThis bill would declare that it is to take effect immediately as a bill providing for appropriations related to the Budget Bill.","digestDate":null,"digestVersion":null,"effective":{"basis":"immediate_effect_flag","date":"2025-09-17","note":"The